Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 15:10:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] v0.39.231: Downloads + Plugins settings sections, real
 backend that had no UI
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

James: "Yes build all the ui" (confirming the Firefox-reference settings
gap pass, after the "where is the rebuild UIs?" exchange surfaced that
accounts/mesh/suite already existed but the defaultStartUrl bug meant he'd
never seen them). Mapped every Firefox category his reference screenshot
named to real backend capability before building anything, per the
non-negotiable: map first, no theater.

Two categories had real, working capability sitting completely unexposed:

- Downloads: cg.downloads.list/clearItem/openFolder have been real IPC
  handlers since 2026-08-24, but no section ever called list or
  openFolder — only privacy.js's bulk clearCompleted. New
  sections/downloads.js is the missing per-item view, plus the same real
  downloadDirectory field General already has.

- Extensions: src/plugins/host.js's list()/disable() existed since
  2026-08-24 with zero IPC exposure. Added plugins:list/plugins:disable
  to ipc/bridge.js (thin wrappers over those same real, pre-existing
  methods) + preload/index.js; list() now also returns
  displayName/description, already on every manifest, never returned
  before. New sections/plugins.js — named "Plugins," not "Extensions and
  themes," because themes have zero backend anywhere in this codebase
  (grepped clear-glass/src and clear-glass/renderer directly, confirmed,
  not assumed). A theme toggle would have been exactly the fabrication
  the non-negotiables forbid.

Also added a small real "Page zoom" control to General, wired to the zoom
plugin's already-real toolbar-command signatures via plugins:invoke
(fire-and-forget by that handler's own documented design, so the toast
confirms the command was sent, not a zoom factor this call can't see).

FOUND, NOT BUILT, surfaced honestly rather than stubbed (recorded as
clear-glass.spec gap FGAP1): no real backend anywhere for search-engine
selection, appearance/theme (dark/light mode), or accessibility settings.
"Language" only exists as the fingerprint-spoofing profile's field,
already covered by sections/fingerprint.js — not a general preference.
backgroundTabDefaults.openInBackground (pre-existing toggle in General)
still has zero real consumer anywhere; reconfirmed directly, left
untouched — building more around it would be inert, not real.

Verified live, not just read from source: real Electron app booted under
Xvfb (--no-sandbox), connected via CDP/Playwright to the actual running
devtools port, opened the real Settings window via
window.ClearGlass.window.openSettings(), rendered all three pages with
real data (6 real installed plugins with real manifest text and "active"
state; live options.get() for the download folder field), then clicked
"Disable" on the zoom plugin's row and confirmed its state flipped to
"disabled" on screen — a real round trip through the new IPC handlers to
the real pluginHost.disable(), not asserted from code reading alone.

clear-glass 3.11.1 -> 3.11.2, all six sync points moved together. No new
registry-components.js entries (plugins:list/plugins:disable are new IPC
routes on the existing namespace, not new registry-tracked components) so
interaction-contract.json's routes are unchanged, only its version.
tests/modules/version-sync-and-registry.test.js's hardcoded 3.11.1
literals bumped to 3.11.2 (30/30 passing). nexus-options-autoboot.test.js
unaffected (15/15 passing).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015CQxu3dHTryg8eHTNWShad
